## 🔄 Alternative File Manager Plugins

### 1. **mini.files** ⭐ (Most Similar to Oil)
- **Repo:** https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim
- **Features:** Column view, edit-as-buffer, cross-directory operations
- **Pros:** Part of mini.nvim ecosystem, very lightweight
- **Cons:** Less mature than oil.nvim
- **Use when:** You want similar workflow but prefer mini.nvim ecosystem

### 2. **neo-tree.nvim** (Traditional Tree View)
- **Repo:** https://github.com/nvim-neo-tree/neo-tree.nvim
- **Features:** Sidebar tree, git status, buffer list, diagnostics
- **Pros:** Rich UI, many integrations, good for project overview
- **Cons:** Different workflow (sidebar vs buffer)
- **Use when:** You prefer traditional IDE-style file tree

### 3. **nvim-tree.lua** (Classic Tree)
- **Repo:** https://github.com/nvim-tree/nvim-tree.lua
- **Features:** Classic sidebar tree, file operations, git integration
- **Pros:** Very popular, stable, feature-rich
- **Cons:** Not as modern as neo-tree
- **Use when:** You want proven, stable tree explorer

### 4. **yazi.nvim** (Terminal File Manager Integration)
- **Repo:** https://github.com/mikavilpas/yazi.nvim
- **Features:** Integrates Yazi terminal file manager
- **Pros:** Full-featured file manager, preview images/videos, blazingly fast
- **Cons:** Requires external tool (yazi)
- **Use when:** You use terminal file managers and want deep integration

### 5. **ranger.nvim** (Ranger Integration)
- **Repo:** https://github.com/kelly-lin/ranger.nvim
- **Features:** Integrates Ranger terminal file manager
- **Pros:** Powerful file manager, miller columns view
- **Cons:** Requires ranger installed
- **Use when:** You're already a Ranger user

### 6. **dirbuf.nvim** (Like Oil, Simpler)
- **Repo:** https://github.com/elihunter173/dirbuf.nvim
- **Features:** Edit filesystem as buffer (like oil)
- **Pros:** Simpler than oil, no dependencies
- **Cons:** Less features than oil
- **Use when:** You want minimal oil-like experience

---

## 🏆 Recommendation

**Keep oil.nvim if:**
- You love vim-style editing for file operations
- You need cross-directory operations
- You want LSP integration for refactoring

**Switch to mini.files if:**
- You prefer lighter plugins
- You're already in mini.nvim ecosystem

**Switch to neo-tree if:**
- You want traditional IDE experience
- You need git status in sidebar
- You prefer mouse-friendly UI

**Switch to yazi.nvim if:**
- You're power user who lives in terminal
- You need image/video previews
- You want blazing fast file operations

---

## 📋 Quick Comparison Table

| Plugin | Style | LSP Integration | Git Status | Cross-dir Ops | Dependencies |
|--------|-------|----------------|------------|---------------|--------------|
| **oil.nvim** | Buffer | ✅ Yes | 🟡 Basic | ✅ Yes | nvim-web-devicons |
| **mini.files** | Column | ❌ No | ❌ No | ✅ Yes | None |
| **neo-tree** | Sidebar | 🟡 Limited | ✅ Rich | ❌ No | nui.nvim, plenary |
| **nvim-tree** | Sidebar | ❌ No | ✅ Yes | ❌ No | nvim-web-devicons |
| **yazi.nvim** | Terminal | ❌ No | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | yazi (external) |

